Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:09:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): sidebar rows of every gateway from the hub
 replica at once; awake owners are ordinary rows [daveey]

Instant session loads, part A. The hub replica is now fresh within about a second
(hermes-hub watch), so:
- the replica rows load from the local read without waiting on per-gateway
  reachability probes (each an SSH round trip); the probes still run in the background;
- a replica owner that published within 180 s is awake: its rows are ordinary
  (open the normal way, show running turns). Older or stale is asleep: cached rows,
  never running, as before;
- the hub-sync poller polls the replica cursor every 2 s and reloads only when it
  moves, plus every 30 s.

Tests: offline-sessions awake/asleep and 180 s edge; hub-sync api (no wait on
probes, fresh live list wins); plugin cursor polling. Renderer suite 11375 passed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
